{"c": null, "r": "I'm designing a Bank class with account management methods—opening accounts, depositing, withdrawing, checking balances, and transferring between accounts. I need to handle validation: ensuring amounts are positive integers, initial balances aren't negative, raising errors for non-existent accounts, and preventing duplicate account creation.

The validation order matters—checking amount validity first ensures a failed call leaves all balances untouched. I'll implement InsufficientFunds as a ValueError subclass, set up a module-level default bank instance with delegating functions, and then run tests to verify everything works.
", "t": [["write_file", "{"path":"D:\\Projects\\local_ai\\strata-lab\\runs\\work\\hermes\\bank-1794053343\\bank.py","content":"\"\"\"Account helpers. Balances are integer cents.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass InsufficientFunds(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised when a withdrawal or transfer exceeds the source balance.\"\"\"\n\n\nclass Bank:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._accounts = {}\n\n    def open_account(self, name, initial=0):\n        if initial < 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"initial balance must be >= 0, got \" + repr(initial))\n        if name in self._accounts:\n            raise ValueError(\"account exists: \" + name)\n        self._accounts[name] = initial\n\n    def deposit(self, name, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0, got \" + repr(amount))\n        if name not in self._accounts:\n            raise KeyError(name)\n        self._accounts[name] += amount\n\n    def withdraw(self, name, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0, got \" + repr(amount))\n        if name not in self._accounts:\n            raise KeyError(name)\n        if self._accounts[name] < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"balance for \" + repr(name) + \" is \" + str(self._accounts[name])\n                + \", cannot withdraw \" + str(amount)\n            )\n        self._accounts[name] -= amount\n\n    def balance(self, name):\n        return self._accounts[name]\n\n    def transfer(self, src, dst, amount):\n        if amount <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"amount must be > 0, got \" + repr(amount))\n        if src == dst:\n            raise ValueError(\"cannot transfer to the same account: \" + repr(src))\n        for name in (src, dst):\n            if name not in self._accounts:\n                raise KeyError(name)\n        if self._accounts[src] < amount:\n            raise InsufficientFunds(\n                \"balance for \" + repr(src) + \" is \" + str(self._accounts[src])\n                + \", cannot transfer \" + str(amount)\n            )\n        self._accounts[src] -= amount\n        self._accounts[dst] += amount\n\n\ndefault_bank = Bank()\n\n\ndef open_account(name, initial=0):\n    return default_bank.open_account(name, initial)\n\n\ndef deposit(name, amount):\n    return default_bank.deposit(name, amount)\n\n\ndef withdraw(name, amount):\n    return default_bank.withdraw(name, amount)\n\n\ndef balance(name):\n    return default_bank.balance(name)\n\n\ndef transfer(src, dst, amount):\n    return default_bank.transfer(src, dst, amount)\n"}"]]}

